WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
Welcome back to the wonderful world of Connie.

2
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:11.080
In this short lesson, I'll show you how to park a conversation when you're waiting on someone, and pick it right back up when you're ready.

3
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:18.480
Sometimes you're helping a contact, but you need to wait on someone else, like another department or a doctor's office, before you can finish.

4
00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.440
Instead of leaving the conversation open, you can simply park it.

5
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:26.520
To park, just click the Park button at the top of the conversation.

6
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.760
Connie will ask what you're waiting on.

7
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.000
Type a quick note, like, waiting on the clinic to fax records.

8
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.000
That's it.

9
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.720
The conversation is parked, and you're free to help someone else.

10
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.360
To find your parked conversations, click the car icon in the left menu.

11
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.000
This is your Parking Lot.

12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.880
Here you'll see every parked conversation for the whole team, who parked it, who the contact is, what they're waiting on, and when.

13
00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:58.240
When you're ready, just click Reactivate, and the conversation comes right back to you, with its full history.

14
00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.680
And because the lot is shared, if you're busy or away, a teammate can pick it up for you.

15
00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.760
Whoever grabs it, owns it.

16
00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:10.120
And if the issue gets resolved another way, there's no need to reopen it.

17
00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.640
Just click Close, right from the lot.

18
00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.080
Just like that, nothing falls through the cracks.

19
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.520
Thanks for using Connie.

20
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.240
We can't wait to see all the amazing things you do with it.
